B.VF=new A.fk("In 1620 a ship called the Mayflower sailed across the ocean from England. It carried about 100 people. They landed on the coast of a place we now call Massachusetts.","story_ship",null)
B.Vz=new A.fk("But the land was not empty. It was home to the Wampanoag people. Wampanoag means People of the First Light. They had lived there for thousands of years in round houses called wetus, and they grew corn, beans and squash.","story_wetu_village",null)
B.VI=new A.fk("The first winter was very hard for the newcomers, and many of them got sick. A Patuxet Wampanoag man named Tisquantum spoke English. He showed them how to plant corn and where to fish.","story_cornfield","char_tisquantum")
B.Vx=new A.fk("In the fall of 1621 the crops were ready. The newcomers held a harvest celebration. The Wampanoag leader, Massasoit, and about 90 Wampanoag men joined about 50 colonists. They ate, played games and visited for three days.","story_harvest_table",null)
B.VJ=new A.fk("People did not call that gathering Thanksgiving back then. Today, Wampanoag people still live in Massachusetts, and families everywhere gather in the fall to give thanks for the harvest and for each other.","story_wetu_village","wampanoag_child_v2")
